# {{plugin_name}}

> {{description}}

A [Cascade](https://github.com/acamarata/cascade) WASM plugin of type **{{plugin_type}}**.

## Requirements

- Rust toolchain + `wasm32-wasip1` target:
  ```
  rustup target add wasm32-wasip1
  ```
- Cascade CLI:
  ```
  cargo install cascade-cli
  ```

## Build

```bash
cargo build --target wasm32-wasip1
# Or use the convenience script:
./build.sh
```

## Test

```bash
cascade plugin test
```

## Install

```bash
./build.sh
cascade plugin enable {{plugin_name}}
```

## Plugin manifest

See `plugin.json` for the plugin configuration. The `permissions` block controls
what system access the plugin has — all are deny-by-default.

## Development

Edit `src/lib.rs` to implement your plugin logic. The `#[cascade_plugin]`
attribute on your struct generates the WASM ABI entry points automatically.

See the [Cascade plugin development guide](https://github.com/acamarata/cascade/wiki/plugin-development-guide)
for the full API reference.
